---
import DocsLayout from '../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
import Callout from '../components/Callout.astro';
import Toc from '../components/Toc.astro';
import { withBase } from '../lib/paths';

const toc = [
	{id: 'flow', label: 'Request flow'},
	{id: 'run', label: 'Run the server'},
	{id: 'env', label: 'Environment'},
	{id: 'responses', label: 'HTTP responses'},
	{id: 'settlement', label: 'Settlement'},
	{id: 'client', label: 'Client'},
];
---

<DocsLayout
	title="Paid scan API"
	eyebrow="[ 10 · x402 ]"
	description="HTTP OSINT Scanner with per-scan payment via x402 on Stellar (Local402), priced in Chilean pesos."
>
	<Toc items={toc} />

	<h2 id="flow">Request flow</h2>
	<pre><code>GET /scan/&lt;CONTRACT_ID&gt;
  → 400  INVALID_CONTRACT_ID   (before paywall — no quote)
  → 402  Payment Required      price in CLP → USDC via Reflector
  → 200  OK                    paid: functions, params, UDTs
  → 404 / 422 / 502 / 500      scan failed after auth — not settled</code></pre>

	<Callout type="warn" title="Scanner only">
		<p>
			Chaos Monkey broadcasts transactions — it stays a local, explicit action and is
			<strong>never</strong> exposed over HTTP. The Local402 route description is:
			<em>“Kuyfi OSINT scan: functions, parameters and types of a Soroban Testnet contract.”</em>
		</p>
	</Callout>

	<h2 id="run">Run the server</h2>
	<pre><code>cp .env.example .env   # set PAY_TO at minimum
npm run build
node --env-file=.env dist/server.js
# or: npm run serve / kuyfi-server

# Startup log:
# kuyfi-server: GET http://localhost:4021/scan/&lt;CONTRACT_ID&gt;</code></pre>
	<p>
		Missing <code>PAY_TO</code> → process prints an error and <code>process.exit(1)</code>.
	</p>

	<h2 id="env">Environment</h2>
	<table>
		<thead>
			<tr>
				<th>Variable</th>
				<th>Default</th>
				<th>Notes</th>
			</tr>
		</thead>
		<tbody>
			<tr>
				<td><code>PAY_TO</code></td>
				<td>required</td>
				<td>Public <code>G…</code> address. Never a secret key.</td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<td><code>PRICE</code></td>
				<td><code>500 CLP</code></td>
				<td>Any Reflector currency, e.g. <code>0.50 USD</code>, <code>0.02 UF</code></td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<td><code>NETWORK</code></td>
				<td><code>stellar:testnet</code></td>
				<td>
					Payment settlement network (<code>stellar:testnet</code> |
					<code>stellar:pubnet</code>). Scans always read Soroban Testnet.
				</td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<td><code>FACILITATOR_URL</code></td>
				<td>derived from NETWORK</td>
				<td>
					Testnet: <code>https://local402.vercel.app/facilitator</code><br />
					Pubnet: <code>https://local402-mainnet.vercel.app/facilitator</code>
					(mainnet facilitator allowlists <code>PAY_TO</code>)
				</td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<td><code>PORT</code></td>
				<td><code>4021</code></td>
				<td></td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<td><code>LOCAL402_QUOTE_SECRET</code></td>
				<td>unset</td>
				<td>
					Only for multi-instance deploys: same random value on every instance so a
					quote from one node is honored by another.
				</td>
			</tr>
		</tbody>
	</table>

	<h2 id="responses">HTTP responses</h2>

	<h3>400 — before paywall</h3>
	<pre><code>&#123;
  "error": "INVALID_CONTRACT_ID",
  "message": "Expected 56 characters starting with C (A-Z, 0-9)."
&#125;</code></pre>

	<h3>200 — paid success</h3>
	<p>
		Body shape from <code>scan_server.ts</code> + <code>toPublicScan()</code>:
	</p>
	<pre><code>&#123;
  "contractId": "C…",
  "network": "testnet",
  "bytecodeSize": 12345,
  // …toPublicScan(scan): functions, udts, etc.
  // Same public scan block shape as SecurityReport.scan
&#125;</code></pre>

	<h3>Scan failures (after payment auth)</h3>
	<table>
		<thead>
			<tr>
				<th>ScanError</th>
				<th>Status</th>
				<th>Body</th>
			</tr>
		</thead>
		<tbody>
			<tr>
				<td><code>CONTRACT_NOT_FOUND</code></td>
				<td><code>404</code></td>
				<td><code>&#123; "error": "CONTRACT_NOT_FOUND" &#125;</code></td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<td><code>XDR_ALIGN_FAILURE</code></td>
				<td><code>422</code></td>
				<td><code>&#123; "error": "XDR_ALIGN_FAILURE" &#125;</code></td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<td><code>RPC_UNAVAILABLE</code></td>
				<td><code>502</code></td>
				<td><code>&#123; "error": "RPC_UNAVAILABLE" &#125;</code></td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<td><code>UNKNOWN</code> / other</td>
				<td><code>500</code></td>
				<td><code>&#123; "error": "UNKNOWN" &#125;</code></td>
			</tr>
		</tbody>
	</table>

	<h2 id="settlement">Settlement rules</h2>
	<ul>
		<li>Malformed Contract ID → <code>400</code> before any price is quoted.</li>
		<li>
			x402 settles only when the handler answers with status &lt; 400. Failed scans
			(<code>404</code>, <code>422</code>, <code>502</code>, <code>500</code>) are
			<strong>not</strong> charged.
		</li>
		<li>
			Payment network (<code>NETWORK</code>) is independent of scan network — OSINT
			always hits Testnet RPC.
		</li>
	</ul>

	<h2 id="client">Client example</h2>
	<pre><code>npx -y local402-client quote http://localhost:4021/scan/&lt;CONTRACT_ID&gt;</code></pre>
	<p>
		For Troubleshoot common 402 / env mistakes →
		<a href={withBase('/troubleshooting')}>Troubleshooting</a>.
	</p>
</DocsLayout>
